WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.150
In Rome, a monk from Britain objects
to a line from Augustine's prayers.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.780
Give what Thou commandest,
and command what Thou wilt.

3
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.140
It troubled him.

4
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:14.280
It seemed to make goodness wait
for God, not for human effort.

5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.370
Yet Matthew's Gospel says:
you shall be perfect,

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.160
just as your Father in heaven is perfect.

7
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.650
So if God commands us to be
perfect, does that mean we can be?

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.780
In this mission, you'll
meet Pelagius, and Arminius,

9
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.890
a Dutch theologian who rejected
Calvin's view of predestination.

10
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.350
Then you'll compare four thinkers on sin,

11
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.290
grace and free will.

12
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: weigh up whether a command
to be perfect means we can obey it.
